Background
The B&H Sell Used page is a primary entry point for customers looking to trade in or sell used gear. A Medallia VoC analysis of seller survey responses identified persistent friction across the selling flow, and GA4 funnel data confirmed significant abandonment before quote completion. A UX audit, competitive analysis (MPB, KEH, Adorama), and a working session with the research team were completed in Q1 2026 to baseline the current state. A lo-fi prototype has been developed incorporating research findings, and a research brief is ready to support concept testing.

Issues
Medallia identifies four primary friction areas in the seller flow: (1) no EFT/Direct Deposit payment option, leaving customers without a preferred payout method; (2) no save-and-return capability, forcing sellers to restart the process if they leave mid-flow; (3) poor payment and valuation transparency — sellers don't understand how quotes are calculated or how accessories affect pricing; and (4) no meaningful communication around used item rejection handling. Additionally, B&H's tax-free trade-in advantage — a meaningful differentiator vs. competitors — is absent from the seller flow entirely, leaving a key trust and conversion signal unleveraged.

Solution
Redesign the Sell Used seller flow to address the top Medallia friction points and incorporate competitive best practices. Specific changes include: adding EFT/Direct Deposit as a fourth payment option, implementing save-and-return at the basket step, introducing valuation transparency copy with price range explanations tied to condition, an accessories checklist with a live subtotal that feeds directly into the quote, and tax-equivalence framing for store credit that communicates B&H's unique trade-in advantage. The lo-fi prototype (bh_sell_used_lofi_v01.html) is the design artifact for the first round of concept testing with Birdie Park Abraham.


